    "narrative": "For LawDog today, we are leaning heavily into favorable pitching matchups to drive volume, highlighted by **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Bryce Harper** (68.19). **Dylan Beavers** earns the highest projection of the day by capitalizing on a soft matchup against Sugano (4.89 xERA) and a massive 14% park-factor boost, making him our priority play. **Bryce Harper** remains the anchor of the lineup despite facing a decent arm in Clarke; his high base projection and favorable #3 spot in the order provide the floor we need to chase wins. **Zack Gelof** (67.85) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (66.49) are also locked in as strong starts, both benefiting from a 19% SP skill boost against mediocre arms in Bradford and Chandler, respectively.\n\nWe are carefully navigating platoon advantages to maximize our efficiency. **Lawrence Butler** (60.94) is trending upward despite a negative platoon split against the lefty Bradford, as his raw power and spot in the heart of the order keep his floor well above the marginal threshold. Conversely, **JJ Bleday** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his score of 48.26 was respectable, a significant -14% penalty due to his dynamic platoon disadvantage against Mize forced him to the bench in favor of higher-efficiency options like **Daulton Varsho** (58.87) and **Justin Crawford** (58.91). **JJ Bleday** remains our primary pivot if any last-minute lineup changes occur.\n\nRisk mitigation is central to today\u2019s strategy, particularly with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (53.31). He remains in the lineup, but his score is suppressed by a tough matchup against Cease (2.97 xERA); he is a \"start your studs\" situation where we accept the lower ceiling to maintain potential for counting stats. With **Tyler Freeman** currently in the minors with Albuquerque and **Will Smith** confirmed out of the lineup, our bench depth is thinner than ideal, meaning we are relying on our core starters to avoid late-scratches. We are closely monitoring the environment for **Dylan Beavers** and **Justin Crawford** to ensure the projected park factors hold up as game time approaches.",
